Cover geometry used (KDP formula): spine = 180 pages x 0.002252 in = 0.4054 in; full cover = 0.125 + 6 + 0.4054 + 6 + 0.125 = 12.6554 in wide x 9.2500 in high (0.125 in bleed all round). Spine text is allowed (more than 79 pages). The 2 x 1.2 in barcode area on the lower right of the back cover is left clear; choose KDP's free ISBN and KDP prints the barcode there.

Interior margins: inside (gutter) 0.75 in, outside 0.6 in, top and bottom 0.75 in — above KDP minimums for 151–300 pages (inside 0.5 in, outside 0.25 in). All fonts embedded.

**Important:** if you change any text, the page count can change. The cover must then be regenerated with the new spine width, or KDP will reject it.

