## Before you publish — action needed

1. **Cover photo resolution.** The background photo in the Canva design is only 1024 x 1024 px. On the paperback front it prints at about 108 ppi; KDP recommends 300. Text is vector and will print sharply, but the photo may look soft and KDP's previewer may warn. Fix: in Canva, *Share > Download > PDF Print* (or supply the original photo at 2,000 px or more), and the cover can be rebuilt with it.
2. **Back-cover copy** (headline, blurb, bullets, author bio) was drafted from your Executive Summary and website; please review the wording. The quote is from Dr. Vicente’s Foreword.
3. **Black & white interior:** figures print in grayscale. If you want colour figures, choose *Premium color* in KDP (higher print cost); the spine factor changes to 0.002347 in/page, so the cover must be regenerated.
